Subject: Preserve the empty-principal SSH certificate fixture

Origin: DHI-internal (dependency compatibility)
Description: Sign with a temporary principal before restoring the empty-principal fixture.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/spiffe/spire.git 746331571d5563bb28bf1dc1c2cd04e1570453d8
Verify: test pkg/common/plugin/sshpop/handshake_test.go::TestVerifyAttestationData
Forwarded: no (upstream main retains the incompatible helper)
Drop-When: never: supported SPIRE release sources are immutable and need this fixture with current x/crypto

Recent x/crypto rejects signing certificates with no principals before SPIRE can exercise its own validation. The helper signs with a temporary principal, clears it afterward, and preserves the production rejection assertion.

diff --git a/pkg/common/plugin/sshpop/handshake_test.go b/pkg/common/plugin/sshpop/handshake_test.go
--- a/pkg/common/plugin/sshpop/handshake_test.go
+++ b/pkg/common/plugin/sshpop/handshake_test.go
@@ -47,2 +47,9 @@ func newTest(t *testing.T, opts ...func(*ssh.Certificate)) *testParams {
-	err = certificate.SignCert(rand.Reader, signer)
-	require.NoError(t, err)
+	hasNoPrincipals := len(certificate.ValidPrincipals) == 0
+	if hasNoPrincipals {
+		certificate.ValidPrincipals = []string{"temporary-principal"}
+	}
+	err = certificate.SignCert(rand.Reader, signer)
+	require.NoError(t, err)
+	if hasNoPrincipals {
+		certificate.ValidPrincipals = nil
+	}
